[align=center]
[size=200][b]Troubleshooting & Recovery[/b][/size]
[/align]
[hr]
[notice][b]Start with the least destructive checks.[/b]
Do not delete working Switch Vision, MQTT or Discovery state simply because something looks wrong.[/notice]

[size=150][b]First checks[/b][/size]
[code]1. Open Switch Vision Installer
2. Use Update All
3. Restart Home Assistant Core if requested
4. Hard-refresh the browser
5. Run Discovery
6. Check Discovery status
7. Use Show Debug only if required[/code]

[size=150][b]Sidebar missing[/b][/size]
Confirm the Switch Vision integration exists, Home Assistant Core was restarted after a Core update, the Native sidebar option is enabled, and the browser is not serving stale frontend data. Incognito/private browsing is a useful cache test.

[size=150][b]Dashboard does not update[/b][/size]
Confirm Discovery completed successfully. The Native panel keeps existing working cards if refresh fails.

[size=150][b]Discovery timeout[/b][/size]
[code]Timeout: 3 seconds
Retries: 1[/code]
Check management address, routing, UDP/161, read-only community and switch ACLs.

[size=150][b]SNMP2MQTT did not start/restart[/b][/size]
Check the final Discovery handoff result. Common causes include no newly generated YAML, YAML validation failure, missing/stale SNMP2MQTT, generated mode disabled, Supervisor access unavailable, or deliberate manual-target mode.
[warning]Current Discovery verifies the handoff and does not treat a restart request alone as proof the new telemetry became active.[/warning]

[size=150][b]Sensors are missing[/b][/size]
Confirm the switch and expected sensors exist in generated SNMP2MQTT configuration, SNMP2MQTT accepted it, MQTT is connected and the sensor prefix matches the card.

[size=150][b]Old SNMP devices remain after moving to UniFi API only[/b][/size]
Use:
[code]Switch Vision Hub → Discovery → SNMP cleanup → Reset SNMP Discovery Data[/code]
Then run Discovery again. This preserves UniFi API data/settings.

[size=150][b]Stale MQTT entities[/b][/size]
Use Switch Vision Maintenance. Recovery uses ownership checks, preview and explicit confirmation. Never delete unrelated Home Assistant MQTT state.

[size=150][b]Wrong port or uplink layout[/b][/size]
Confirm the exact detected SKU first. For unsupported/incomplete hardware, use Support My Switch rather than guessing the mapping.

[size=150][b]Support My Switch says REVIEW REQUIRED[/b][/size]
Read:
[code]BUNDLE_QUALITY.txt
SANITIZATION_REPORT.txt[/code]
Correct/remove the problem source and create a new contribution.

[size=150][b]Still stuck?[/b][/size]
[url=https://switch-vision.zemerdon.com/viewtopic.php?t=71]Switch Vision Support Request Template[/url]
